  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#47694\", \"PowerToys#23857\", \"PowerToys#47537\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. The Power Display flyout (PowerToys#47694) and the Quick Access tray flyout (PowerToys#23857) always open at the bottom right of the screen, regardless of where the taskbar is docked. In #47694 a maintainer said the bottom-right placement is by design and treated it as a feature request, so there is no setting or fix to apply yet. In #23857 the report was marked as a duplicate of #23772 and described as fixed in a hotfix in early February 2023, so check that you are on a current PowerToys version. If your flyouts still open at the bottom right with a side or top taskbar, add your use case and a thumbs-up to #47694 so it can be prioritised. In #47537, a user whose flyout opened in the middle of the screen found the cause was a Windhawk mod that centres new windows. If you use Windhawk, check for that.\"}",
